            <ArticleTitle>The effectiveness of EMG biofeedback training in low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eighteen patients with chronic low back pain (lbp) of muscle tension origin were given an EMG biofeedback training. Compared to seven controls they showed a significant decrease during training in muscle tension and subsequently in pain. However, at follow-up EMG levels dropped to the initial (high) level. Pain scores of patients with high pain decrements during training showed further improvement during follow-up, which was not the case with patients showing less substantial improvement. The importance of cognitions was discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
